>>>> +        if ((s->prefix & PREFIX_EVEX) && !validate_evex_apx(s, 
>>>> decode)) {
>>>> +            return false;
>>>> +        }
>>>
>>> They're only reached by map4, so surely
>>>
>>>       assert(s->prefix & PREFIX_EVEX);
>>>
>>> is more appropriate, and the subsequent test for evex moot.
>>
>> No, validate_vex() is also invoked for non-VEX/EVEX instructions.
> 
> Of course.  But how do you get X86_EVEX_APX* from non EVEX paths?
 From decode_group* where it is shared between normal and EVEX paths. 
For example decode_group1 (ALU operation with a memory and an immediate 
operand) and can set X86_EVEX_APX_cmp, and decode_group{3,4_5} can set 
X86_EVEX_APX.

